## 1. Deliverables & Technical Architecture

### 1. Browser Domain Models (`src/browser/models.py`)
- Pydantic domain data models (strictly decoupled from Qt Widgets):
  - `BrowserSecurityLevel`: Enum (`STRICT`, `STANDARD`, `PERMISSIVE`).
  - `NavigationState`: Navigation model (`url`, `title`, `is_loading`, `progress`, `is_secure`, `can_go_back`, `can_go_forward`).
  - `BrowserTabModel`: Tab representation model (`id`, `url`, `title`, `icon_url`, `is_pinned`, `is_muted`, `security_level`).
  - `BrowserProfile`: Storage profile model (`profile_id`, `name`, `data_dir`, `cache_dir`, `cookies_dir`, `history_dir`, `downloads_dir`, `sessions_dir`).
  - `BrowserSession`: Session state model (`session_id`, `workspace_id`, `open_tabs`, `active_tab_index`, `updated_at`).

### 2. Browser Interface Contracts (`src/browser/protocols.py`)
- `@runtime_checkable` Protocol interfaces:
  - `IBrowserProfile`
  - `IBrowserSessionManager`
  - `IBrowserHistory`
  - `IBrowserSecurityPolicy`
  - `IBrowserService`

### 3. Profile & Storage Infrastructure (`src/browser/profile_manager.py`)
- `BrowserProfileManager`: Workspace-isolated directory structure manager:
  - Paths: `data/browser/profiles/{profile_id}/` (`cache/`, `cookies/`, `history/`, `downloads/`, `sessions/`).
  - Strict profile isolation preventing data bleed across workspaces.

### 4. Session Manager (`src/browser/session_manager.py`)
- `BrowserSessionManager`: Manages saving, loading, restoring, closing, and workspace switching using atomic `JsonStore` persistence with graceful fallback for corrupted session files.

### 5. Browser Service & URL Normalization (`src/browser/service.py`)
- `BrowserService`: Implementation of `IBrowserService`:
  - **URL Normalization**: Handles raw inputs (`google.com` $\rightarrow$ `https://google.com`, `localhost:8000` $\rightarrow$ `http://localhost:8000`, `192.168.1.1` $\rightarrow$ `https://192.168.1.1`).
  - **Search Query Detection**: Automatically detects multi-word queries (e.g. `python pyside6 tutorial`) and constructs DuckDuckGo search URLs (`https://duckduckgo.com/?q=...`).
  - Tab management, session coordination, cache/cookie cleanup.

### 6. Security Policy Specification (`docs/browser_security_policy.md`)
- Documented Zero-Trust security rules:
  - Camera: Disabled
  - Microphone: Disabled
  - Notifications: Disabled
  - Geolocation: Disabled
  - Clipboard Read: Ask
  - Clipboard Write: Allowed
  - JavaScript: Enabled
  - PDF Viewer: Enabled
  - Popups: Blocked

